# Vercel does NOT apply .gitignore. Without this file every path in the working
# directory is uploaded and served, which is how answers/ — including internal
# reports and third-party source PDFs — became publicly reachable after the
# 1.0.4 deployment. Everything listed here is local working material and must
# never leave this machine.

# Local working notes, research and internal reports.
answers/

# Internal tooling source. `tools/` ships in the release package because the
# archive has to be able to verify itself, but the website never serves it: the
# deploy smoke test lists the private paths it asserts are absent, so serving it
# published that inventory. Git and the release ZIP keep it; the site does not.
tools/

# Withdrawn drafts and local-only material, mirrored from .gitignore.
md/
licensing/
archive/
openbranddefinition-site-*-public-draft/

# The trailing slash above matches the unpacked directory only, so the companion
# archive `openbranddefinition-site-0.9.5-public-draft.zip` stayed in the upload
# and was served publicly. Root-anchored, so the published release archives under
# spec/<version>/OBDS-<version>-FINAL.zip are untouched; deploy-smoke-test.py
# asserts both halves of that.
/*.zip

# Environments and caches.
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.eggs/

# Local tool configuration. Gitignored, so it never reaches GitHub, but Vercel
# does not read .gitignore: without this line `.claude/settings.local.json` was
# served publicly. Same failure mode as `answers/` before 1.1.2.
.claude/

# Hosting and secrets.
.vercel
.env*
.DS_Store

# Internal candidate evidence, never a public surface.
release-work/

# The non-public Task Facts audit store. `reference/` is served, so without these
# lines the 485 historical research and ratification records under
# reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/, the inventory that lists them and the
# Historical Audit Evidence Registry would all be publicly reachable. Same
# failure mode as answers/ after 1.0.4, and the same fix.
#
# The release archive already excludes them: `public_package_member()` in
# reference/release-gate.py ships only the four evaluator sources named by
# reference/task-facts/1.0/PUBLIC-EVIDENCE-MANIFEST.json. These lines make the
# deployment agree with the package.
#
# No negation. 4.1.0 first shipped this as `evidence/**` plus four `!` lines
# re-including the public four. Git honours that; Vercel does not. The 4.1.0
# deployment dropped the whole subtree and served all four as 404, which is the
# harmless direction but still wrong. So every excluded path is now named
# outright: a directory when nothing public lives beneath it, a literal file
# path otherwise. 27 lines cover all 481 non-public records, and the four
# authorised sources are simply never mentioned.
#
# Derived from the store itself, not written by hand. To regenerate after any
# change to the store, exclude each directory with no public descendant and
# enumerate the non-public files in the directories that have one.
reference/task-facts/1.0/EVIDENCE-MANIFEST.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/HISTORICAL-AUDIT-REGISTRY.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/evaluation-evidence/
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/frozen-contract/
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/frozen-contract-integrity.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/FROZEN-MANIFEST.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/PROVENANCE.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/README.md
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/package.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/regression-results.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/results.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/run-fixtures.mjs
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/test-results.txt
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node/test.mjs
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-node-integrity.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/FROZEN-MANIFEST.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/README.md
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/provenance.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/results.json
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/test-output.txt
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python/test_evaluate.py
reference/task-facts/1.0/evidence/interop/cycles/cycle-1/implementation-python-integrity.json
